      "id": "search",
      "title": "Results from another time",
      "subtitle": "The last response isn't the latest search.",
      "category": "Response ordering",
      "difficulty": "Tricky",
      "goal": "Show results for an older query while the search box says react.",
      "hint": "Search for re, then react. A network response can arrive out of order.",
      "explanation": "Both searches update the same results state when their promises resolve. A slower response for re arrives after react and overwrites the relevant results. A monotonically increasing request sequence lets the fix ignore outdated responses.",
